course: dictionary
lesson: 1073
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word bow is one of them. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning to use. Read the words around it and ask: what would make sense here?
explain: Listen to how it sounds. A knot and a bent stick rhyme with «go». Bending your body to say thank you, and the front of a ship, rhyme with «cow».
explain: «A magician in Dublin made a girl's watch vanish, and then he gave it straight back with a bow.» Here a bow means bending the body forward to show thanks, not a knot or a stick. The word «bow» tells you what he did.
fact: Bow has four main meanings: a knot with loops, a bent stick for arrows or violins, bending forward to show respect, and the front of a ship.
fact: «Bow» (rhymes with «go») can mean a knot with two loops made from ribbon or laces.
fact: «Bow» (rhymes with «cow») can mean to bend your head or body forward to say thank you or show respect.
fact: A violin bow is a stick with hairs, and rosin is rubbed on the hair so it grips the strings.
exercise: «She tied a bow in her ribbon.» What is a bow here? | Bending forward to say thank you | The front part of a ship | *A knot with two loops | A bent stick for shooting arrows
exercise: «The actor came back on stage to take a bow.» What does take a bow mean? | *Bend forward to thank the audience | Shoot an arrow at the target | Tie a knot in the rope | Sail to the front of the ship
exercise: Mum has 12 metres of ribbon and uses 2 metres for each bow. How many bows can she make? | 4 | 10 | *6 | 24
test: «The ship's bow hit the waves.» What is the bow? | A loop of ribbon | A knot at the back of the boat | *The front part of the ship | A hairy stick for playing the violin
test: The word «bow» for a knot rhymes with which word? | *Rhymes with go | Rhymes with cow | It does not rhyme with any word | Rhymes with bee
exam: «Robin Hood carried a bow and arrows into the forest.» What is a bow here? | A knot with two loops | *A bent stick with a string for shooting arrows | The front part of a ship | Bending forward to show respect
